{"title":"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>UNM - PNM STATEWIDE MATHEMATICS CONTEST XLVII. February 7, 2015. Second Round. Three Hours\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Problem_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Problem_3\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 3</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Problem_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 4</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Problem_5\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 5</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Problem_6\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">6</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 6</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Problem_7\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">7</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 7</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#Problem_8\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">8</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 8</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-9\"><a href=\"#Problem_9\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">9</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 9</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-10\"><a href=\"#Problem_10\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">10</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem 10</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-11\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">11</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_1\">Problem 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the sequence\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/a/e/faef8c51a0ae8fcca504f937386978a5caf8cc55.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1, 2, 2, 4, 4, 4, 4, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, 8, \\cdots$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"277\" height=\"16\" />\nwhat number occupies position <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/7/c/b7c41d5d55f66cd4a292a064c28c0c679742c8a6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2015$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"35\" height=\"13\" />?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 1\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_2\">Problem 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> is a set of finitely many non-collinear points in the plane (i.e., not all of\nthe points are on the same line), then there is a line which contains exactly two of the\npoints of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Is the claim true if <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> has infinitely many points? Hint: Use an extremal\nconfiguration.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 2\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_3\">Problem 3</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 3\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Show that the bisect of an angle in a triangle divides the opposite side in segments whose\nlengths have the same ratio as the ratio of the adjacent sides,\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/c/4/cc4046d24edd6833365b1eefa3a0fc2836a4ed97.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[AN/NB = CA/CB\\]\" width=\"157\" height=\"18\" />\nin the picture below. NOTE: The same is true for the bisector of an exterior angle of a\ntriangle, i.e., it divides the opposite side externally into segments that are proportional\nto the adjacent sides. You do not have to write a proof of this fact.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 3\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_4\">Problem 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>There are <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/f/edf074831eb5bc9e61d6d6e09f525a86e3068f6a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$12$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> coins in a parking meter and we know that one of them is counterfeit. The\ncounterfeit coin is either heavier or lighter than the others. How can we find the fake coin\nand also if it is heavier or lighter in three weighings using a balance scale? Hint: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/f/aaf6c0b8c2b93585688f438000a146dda4e97920.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$4=3+1$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"76\" height=\"15\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 4\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_5\">Problem 5</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 5\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/5/ff5fb3d775862e2123b007eb4373ff6cc1a34d4e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" /> be two points in the plane. Describe the set <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> of all points in the plane such\nthat for any point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/4/4b4cade9ca8a2c8311fafcf040bc5b15ca507f52.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> in <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/2/ad28c83c99a8fd0dd2e2e594c9d02ee532765a0a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" /> we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/6/7/567f77f7d9f28dbc842bacdfaae59134af4cdd33.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[|PA| = 3|PB|\\]\" width=\"106\" height=\"18\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 5\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_6\">Problem 6</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 6\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>A faulty calculator displayed <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/5/7/d5734bdac609160dab2e628e7dc3983c2927a410.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\diamond 38 \\diamond 1625$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"80\" height=\"13\" /> as an output of a calculation. We know that\ntwo of the digits of this number are missing and these are replaced with the symbol <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/6/4/a64597fa971a2a89feef230c4a309e18d2bb0c8f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\diamond$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" />.\nFurthermore, we know that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/2/bf2c9074b396e3af0dea52d792660eea1c77f10f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$9$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/6/8/c6878713578626763c38433b3f4c8c2205ad0c15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$11$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"20\" height=\"14\" /> divide the computed output. What are the missing\ndigits and the complete output of our calculation?\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 6\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_7\">Problem 7</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 7\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> be the average of the three numbers <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/2/b/12b3565ecbec7de542b3290268b12d88d759a522.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\sin{2\\alpha}, \\sin{2\\beta} , \\sin(2\\gamma)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"162\" height=\"18\" /> where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/e/1/2e1ea02bafb00d96b69babd26e3bf3dd115cd156.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\alpha + \\beta + \\gamma = \\pi.$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"116\" height=\"16\" />\nExpress the product <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/f/1/0f1156b737a090f19124e417ba4850b475e24357.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P = sin(\\alpha) sin(\\beta) sin(\\gamma)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"190\" height=\"18\" /> in terms of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/9/019e9892786e493964e145e7c5cf7b700314e53b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 7\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_8\">Problem 8</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 8\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose we draw circles of radius <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> with centers at every point in the plane with integer\ncoordinates. What is the smallest <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> such that every line with slope <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/f/c/ffce6d6b648c3d71987ef57d600fb349d5a0e318.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2/7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"27\" height=\"18\" /> has a point in\ncommon with at least one of these circles?\n</p><p><br />\n<a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 8\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_9\">Problem 9</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=9\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 9\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>What is the probability of picking at random three points on a circle of radius one so that\nall three lie in a semicircle?\n</p><p>[2015 [UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 9|Solution]]\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem_10\">Problem 10</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=10\" title=\"Edit section: Problem 10\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Solve <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/2/c323b760b58adfa04e8b65227faed0727f24e64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\underbrace{\\overline{aa\\ldots a}}_{\\text{2k}} - \\underbrace{\\overline{bb\\ldots b}}_{\\text{k}}=(\\underbrace{\\overline{cc\\ldots c}}_{\\text{k}})^2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"222\" height=\"39\" />\n, where <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/a/5/aa523911acabdd784ea4736cf8d3d9267fe561dd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(\\underbrace{\\overline{cc\\ldots c}}_{\\text{k}}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -25px\" width=\"60\" height=\"40\" />\ndenotes a number with <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/c/3/8c325612684d41304b9751c175df7bcc0f61f64f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$k$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"14\" /> digits each one\nequal to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/3/7/3372c1cb6d68cf97c2d231acc0b47b95a9ed04cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$c$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"10\" height=\"10\" />.\n</p><p><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2015 UNM-PNM Statewide High School Mathematics Contest II Problems/Problem 10\">Solution</a>\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2015_UNM-PNM_Statewide_High_School_Mathematics_Contest_II_Problems&amp;action=edit&amp;section=11\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261018060847\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.022 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.036 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 192/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 0/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 2/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 5508/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    0.000      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:17066:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261018060847 and revision id 100283. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}